KNOWNBUG
main.cpp
--cpp17
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
--
KNOWNBUG: N5008 [temp.variadic]/5 + [dcl.init.aggr].  A variadic function
template whose body expands a pack of CALLS inside a BRACED (aggregate)
initializer (`return box2{fwd(e)...}`) -- the shape of libstdc++ std::make_tuple
/ the tuple forwarding constructor.  The pack `e` inside `fwd(e)...` is
substituted to `e$0, e$1` as arguments of a SINGLE `fwd(...)` call (retaining
the `...`) instead of replicating `fwd(e)` per element to `fwd(e$0), fwd(e$1)`;
the malformed body then fails to convert and is DROPPED ("no body for callee
mk<int,int>"), so the call returns a nondeterministic value and the assertion
fails (VERIFICATION FAILED / EXIT=10 -- does NOT match the desired SUCCESSFUL
above, so a known bug).  The SAME call-pack inside a function-CALL argument list
(`sum(fwd(e)...)`) is handled, as is a braced init without a call (`box2{e...}`);
the defect is specific to a call-pack inside a braced/aggregate initializer.
This is the root of cpp17_tuple_basic (std::make_tuple<int,int,int> is left
without a body -> std::get reads garbage).  g++ runs {10,20}; clang++ accepts.
Flip to CORE once a call-pack in a braced initializer is expanded in a deferred
body.
